<title>SWITZERLAND: Use Swiss shares for Germany play - CS.</title>
<headline>Use Swiss shares for Germany play - CS.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>CS Holding said investors could profit by buying shares of undervalued Swiss companies that stand to benefit from an a German economic upswing and persistent Swiss franc weakness against the mark.</p>
<p>In a research note, it recommended purchasing decor company Forbo Holding SA, machinery maker Georg Fischer AG and Kermaik Holding AG for overweighting.</p>
<p>It gave this projections for earnings:</p>
<p>				     1995     1996E    1997E    1998E</p>
<p>Forbo</p>
<p>     -Net income (million Sfr) 56	 59	 65	 70</p>
<p>     -EPS (Sfr)		    38	 40	 45	 48</p>
<p>     -P/E			    13.9     12.7     11.5     10.8</p>
<p>     -Sales in Germany		  25 Percent</p>
<p>Georg Fischer</p>
<p>     -Net income (million Sfr) 65	 58	 74	 89</p>
<p>     -EPS (Sfr)		   101	90	 115	138</p>
<p>     -P/E			    13.1     14.7     11.4     9.6</p>
<p>     -Sales in Germany		  35 Percent</p>
<p>Keramik Laufen</p>
<p>     -Net income (million Sfr) 52	 30	 52	 55</p>
<p>     -EPS (Sfr)		    69	 41	 69	 74</p>
<p>     -P/E			    11.6     19.1     11.2     10.5</p>
<p>     -Sales in Germany		  12 Percent</p>
<p>-- Zurich newsroom +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
